 "note": "Quick, Draw! mermaid 6332888129732608, drawn reclining with the head at upper left and the tail curling up at the right, which is how the mermaid lies in the film. Stroke 0 is the fish body and tail: it runs from the waist down and right, rises into an upright fin and ends in a second fin lobe at the far right. Strokes 1 and 2 are the waistband where the body meets the tail. Stroke 3 is the head, the long hair falling at the left, and the arm: vertices 13 to 17 are the arm reaching out to the right from the shoulder. Strokes 4, 5 and 6 are hair lines across the top of the head. The whole drawing is placed by the head and the tail end and held at one size; only the arm turns at the shoulder, so it rises overhead, comes down to the chest and face, and stretches out to the right as the film's arm does.",
